# ── Query ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^maker retrieves online fixings for the trade$"
    When get '/trades/{id}/fixings/online' with path parameter 'id' from stored variable 'createdTradeId' as user 'maker'
    And attach the response body to the report

# ── Outcomes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The online fixings: 200 + the recording (data.fixings ignored: its dates fill as they pass), kept to compare with
# the trade afterwards.
@Then "^the online fixings of the trade are returned$"
    Then the 'online fixings' are retrieved successfully
    And store response field 'data.fixings' as 'onlineFixings'

# On the trade retrieved after the online fixings: they are stored on the trade as returned.
@Then "^the trade holds the online fixings$"
    Then response status code is '200'
    And response body contains a key 'data.fixings' with stored variable 'onlineFixings'

# On the same trade: every schedule date up to today (the schedule is the gold source) has a fixing value, for each
# fixing source. Where the schedule's fixing dates are is request.fixingDates of data/api/trade_fixings.json (the
# default in defaults, a product's own in its byProduct); a product with several sources names them there
# (request.fixingSources).
@Then "^every fixing date up to today has a value$"
    Then every date at the stored path 'fixingDates' up to today has a fixing value
